# 4. Intro Locations

The purpose of `Intro Locations` is to let me visually define the exact positions used by the intro script instead of describing coordinates or positions to the implementation AI.

The available location markers must be generated from the actual loaded intro script.

**Do not hardcode the marker list into the editor UI.**

When the intro script/configuration is loaded, inspect its declared location markers and generate an editor entry for every required position.

For example, if the intro sequence declares:

`INTRO_PLAYER_START`

`INTRO_MITCHY_START`

`INTRO_MITCHY_TALK_POSITION`

`INTRO_MITCHY_EXIT`

the **Intro Locations** editor automatically shows those four entries.

If another marker is later added to the intro script, it should automatically appear in this editor without requiring a separate UI implementation.

